                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_02\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit adds an early-return guard (`if (udts.isEmpty()) { return; }`) to `BulkLoader.loadUserTypes()` and simplifies the trailing recursive call, because the previous logic threw a spurious `RuntimeException(\"Unable to load user types [])\")` whenever a keyspace had zero user-defined types. The root cause is that when `udts` is empty, the `for` loop never runs, so `notLoaded` stays empty, and the check `notLoaded.size() == udts.size()` evaluates to `0 == 0` (true), incorrectly triggering the \"unable to load\" exception instead of recognizing there was simply nothing to load.\n\ncandidate_01 only creates the initial `BulkLoader.java` (plus build/script changes) and does not yet contain a `loadUserTypes` method at all, so the bug cannot have existed there.\n\ncandidate_02 introduces the entire `loadUserTypes(Collection<UserType> udts, KSMetaData ks)` method verbatim with the flawed logic:\n```java\nprivate static void loadUserTypes(Collection<UserType> udts, KSMetaData ks) {\n    LinkedList<UserType> notLoaded = new LinkedList<UserType>();\n    for (UserType ut : udts) { ... }\n    if (notLoaded.size() == udts.size()) {\n        throw new RuntimeException(\"Unable to load user types \" + notLoaded);\n    }\n    if (notLoaded.size() > 0) {\n        loadUserTypes(notLoaded, ks);\n    }\n}\n```\nThis is exactly the code the fix commit patches (same pre-image, same line numbers), and it is also called unconditionally from the constructor via `loadUserTypes(keyspaceMetadata.getUserTypes(), ksMetaData);` \u2014 meaning any keyspace with no user types would immediately hit the bug. This is the first point at which the problematic code exists, so candidate_02 is the bug-introducing commit.\n\ncandidate_03's diff is identical (same before/after blob hashes) to the actual fix_commit_diff.txt provided \u2014 it is the fix itself, not a bug-introducing candidate, so it is excluded from consideration.\n"
